**Theorem 6.3 (Systematic Drift Toward Truth)**  
*Statement:* With confidence modulation, recovery velocity is amplified toward the true post‑swan equilibrium.

*Proof:* The drift term in the weight SDE includes a component \(\beta_c (\kappa_a - \bar{\kappa})\). For agents holding the correct belief, \(\kappa_a\) is high while the majority’s \(\bar{\kappa}\) is initially low; thus \(\kappa_a - \bar{\kappa} > 0\), giving an additional positive push on the weight update. Conversely, incorrect agents receive a negative push. Summing over all agents, the net drift vector points toward the correct equilibrium. This increases the rate of weight change in the correct direction compared to a system without confidence modulation, thereby increasing \(v_{\text{recovery}}\). \(\square\)

